From: ROCKNIX beryllium port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: beryllium: give Bluetooth a fixed BD address

The WCN3990 on beryllium has no valid stored Bluetooth address (same as the
WiFi random-MAC situation). WiFi copes by generating a random MAC, but the QCA
Bluetooth controller refuses to initialise without a valid BD address: hci0 comes
up "DOWN RAW" and `hciconfig hci0 up` fails with "Operation not supported". Give
it a fixed, locally-administered address via local-bd-address so hci_qca can
program it and the controller initialises.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
@@ -835,6 +835,7 @@
 		vddrf-supply = <&vreg_l17a_1p3>;
 		vddch0-supply = <&vreg_l25a_3p3>;
 		max-speed = <3200000>;
+		local-bd-address = [ 02 00 00 f1 be ba ];
 	};
 };
